{"qid":"Q55502","names":["Kingdom of Jerusalem"],"title":"Kingdom of Jerusalem","endonym":{"native":"مملكة القدس","lang":"ar"},"capsule":"The Kingdom of Jerusalem was a Crusader state established in 1099 when the First Crusade captured Jerusalem and the leaders offered the crown to Godfrey of Bouillon, who accepted the title Advocatus Sancti Sepulchri rather than king. At its apogee under Baldwin I and Baldwin II in the early twelfth century the kingdom extended from the Sinai to beyond the Jordan, supported by the military orders (Templars, Hospitallers) and Italian merchant communes. Saladin's victory at the Battle of Hattin on 4 July 1187 and subsequent capture of Jerusalem reduced the kingdom to a coastal rump; the Third Crusade (1189–1192) under Richard I of England recovered the coast but not the city. The kingdom persisted in name with its capital at Acre until the Mamluk siege of Acre in 1291, with a residual claim held by the kings of Cyprus until 1489.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. The kingdom's territorial extent is documented in considerable detail through Crusader charters, Muslim geographers, and later Frankish legal texts; however precise boundary lines varied rapidly with military fortunes and are estimated rather than mapped contemporaneously.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Kingdom of Jerusalem","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Jerusalem"},{"label":"Britannica: Kingdom of Jerusalem","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Kingdom-of-Jerusalem"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Battle of Hattin","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Hattin"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Siege of Acre (1291)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siege_of_Acre_(1291)"}],"britannica":"place/kingdom-of-Jerusalem","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Kingdom of Jerusalem","rulers":[{"qid":null,"name":"Godfrey of Bouillon","nativeName":"Godefroy de Bouillon","roman":"","start":1099,"end":1100,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Baldwin I","nativeName":"Baudouin Ier","roman":"","start":1100,"end":1118,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Baldwin II","nativeName":"Baudouin II","roman":"","start":1118,"end":1131,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Fulk","nativeName":"Foulque d'Anjou","roman":"","start":1131,"end":1143,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Baldwin III","nativeName":"Baudouin III","roman":"","start":1143,"end":1163,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Amalric I","nativeName":"Amaury Ier","roman":"","start":1163,"end":1174,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Baldwin IV \"the Leper King\"","nativeName":"Baudouin IV le Lépreux","roman":"","start":1174,"end":1185,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Baldwin V","nativeName":"Baudouin V","roman":"","start":1185,"end":1186,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Guy of Lusignan","nativeName":"Guy de Lusignan","roman":"","start":1186,"end":1192,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Conrad of Montferrat","nativeName":"Conrad de Montferrat","roman":"","start":1192,"end":1192,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Henry II of Champagne","nativeName":"Henri II de Champagne","roman":"","start":1192,"end":1197,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Amalric II of Lusignan","nativeName":"Amaury II de Lusignan","roman":"","start":1197,"end":1205,"image":null,"im